From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Feinberg <uge@persimmons.ai>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:51:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] &nf -t: per-output required times under -l; -B/-G and
 ABC_PHYSMAP_GATEMAP

-t: each output's required time is its own arrival x (100+R)/100 instead
of the global critical delay (Nf_ManSetOutputRequireds), so area recovery
cannot deepen non-critical cones. Works with -l (load-aware delays).

-B <rounds>: barycenter AIG placement; per-node wire caps from fanout-star
HPWL, rescaled to the fanout model's mean (needs -l).
-G <file>: per-node wire caps "<gia_obj_id> <cap_fF>" from a placement of
a previous mapping (needs -l).
ABC_PHYSMAP_GATEMAP=<file>: write_verilog emits "<instance> <gia_obj_id>"
so a placement can be joined back to AIG nodes.

All off unless requested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
